# 3. PARTY DEATH RULE

A Dungeon Party has a permanent combat state during the mission.

Example:

```text
PARTY 1

Hero A — Alive
Hero B — Alive
Hero C — Alive
Hero D — Alive
Hero E — Alive
```

If one Hero dies:

```text
Hero A — DEAD
Hero B — Alive
Hero C — Alive
Hero D — Alive
Hero E — Alive
```

The Party can continue if the Dungeon Mission allows it.

However:

# **IF ALL PARTY MEMBERS DIE, THE MISSION FAILS.**

```text
Hero A — DEAD
Hero B — DEAD
Hero C — DEAD
Hero D — DEAD
Hero E — DEAD
        ↓
PARTY DEFEATED
        ↓
MISSION FAILED
        ↓
QUEST FAILED
```

If the Party Leader dies but other members remain alive:

```text
LEADER DEAD
     ↓
PARTY STILL ACTIVE
     ↓
AI / PARTY SYSTEM
     ↓
NEW COMBAT LEADERSHIP LOGIC
```

The death of the Leader alone does **not automatically fail the mission**.

Mission failure occurs when:

```text
ALL ACTIVE HEROES IN THE PARTY
=
DEAD
```

unless a special Floor rule defines another failure condition.

