# 71. FINAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The Dungeon System is not simply a collection of combat stages.

Each Floor represents a fragment of Aetheria.

The Master provides the strategy.

The Party enters the mission.

Once the mission starts, the Party becomes committed to the mission.

```text
MASTER
   ↓
SELECT PARTY
   ↓
ENTER FLOOR
   ↓
PARTY LOCK
   ↓
MISSION
   ↓
COMBAT / EXPLORATION
   ↓
ENEMY SYSTEM
   ↓
EVENT
   ↓
BOSS / RAID
   ↓
VICTORY / FAILURE
   ↓
RNG
   ↓
INVENTORY
   ↓
GAME STATE
   ↓
DATABASE
   ↓
FAIRY REPORT
```

The Master cannot simply remove a Party when the situation becomes dangerous.

The Heroes must face the consequences of the mission.

```text
PARTY ENTERS
     ↓
NO MANUAL EXIT
     ↓
HEROES FIGHT
     ↓
HEROES SURVIVE
     │
     └──────────────► VICTORY

OR

HEROES FALL
     ↓
ALL HEROES DEAD
     ↓
PARTY DEFEATED
     ↓
MISSION FAILED
     ↓
QUEST FAILED
```

The Dungeon therefore becomes a real strategic risk.

Every deployment matters.

Every Hero matters.

Every Party decision matters.

And when the Master sends a Party into the Tower:

> **There is no simple "exit" button.**

> **The Party must finish the mission—or fall inside it.**
